# Core (workspace)

Extends `engineering-kernel.mdc`; portable slice is `rule:engineering-conduct`. This file is the hub-environment remainder.

Venv `$HOME/.venvs/universal` (3.12); `libs/` on PYTHONPATH via `sitecustomize.py` (`from process_ipc.core import ...`).

**`tmp/` is ephemeral** — ¬ persist, ¬ commit. `tmp/prompts/` holds specs/handoffs; `tmp/summaries/` and `/tmp/summaries/` are lead-seat scratch, never a cursor-sdk deliverable. Durable knowledge → `cortex://` or `workspaces://`.

**Observability:** Event Service first (`scripts/query-events --op <name>`; MCP `observability(...)`); logs are fallback. Sole maintainers: gateway, stargate, inference_djinn, process_ipc, event_bus, logging, transport, protocol.

## Lifecycle authority — by WHAT and SCOPE, ¬ tool name

`fleet_service ⇔ listed by manage(action="status")` (gateway, stargate, mcp, rag, cortex_api, agent_bus, event_service, cloud_proxy, git_integration_worker, email_bridge, cdp_ask, …) ⇒ `manage` is their **sole** lifecycle substrate; bypassing it can truncate an in-flight dispatch. `auxiliary ⇔ a --user unit the seat authored that manage does not list` ⇒ the seat manages it. **Unsure ⇒ fleet ⇒ `manage`.**

| Allowed | Forbidden | Gated |
|---|---|---|
| read / analyze / search / propose; fleet lifecycle via `manage`; routine in-tree commits; `systemctl --user` on auxiliary units | `systemctl` at system scope; `systemctl` / `pkill` / `docker restart|stop` against any fleet service; shell mutations outside the edit/commit flow | `git_integrate` / `git_land` |

Output: artifacts (code, UML, verification), ¬ summaries unless asked. Close: `session-close.mdc`.
